course: dictionary
lesson: 4469
title: Harmful and harmless
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Harmful is an adjective. It means causing harm: it can hurt people, animals, plants or things, or make them ill. If something can do harm, it is harmful.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Too much vitamin A can be harmful, so cod-liver oil should not be doubled up with other vitamin A supplements.» The sentence warns you that too much is bad for you, so harmful means it can make you ill. Check by swapping in "bad for you": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The opposite of harmful is harmless, which means it cannot cause harm. Harmful is not only about bodies. Harmful words can hurt feelings as much as hitting, and harmful things can also include poisons, pollution and some unsafe websites.
fact: Harmful means causing harm: hurting or making someone or something ill.
fact: Harmful is an adjective. Its forms are harmful, more harmful and most harmful.
fact: The opposite of harmful is harmless.
fact: Labels on poisons and cleaning products often say «harmful if swallowed».
fact: Pollution and plastic are harmful to wildlife and the environment.
exercise: «Too much vitamin A can be harmful.» What does harmful mean here? | Good for your health | Tasty and sweet | Very large | *Able to make you ill or hurt you
exercise: Which word means the opposite of harmful? | *Harmless | Careful | Hurtful | Dangerous
exercise: Which of these is harmful to wildlife? | *Plastic dumped in the sea | A bird's nest in a tree | Clean rainwater in a pond
test: Mum says the cleaning spray is harmful if swallowed. What does that tell you? | It smells nice, so it is safe to drink | It helps keep your teeth clean | *It can hurt you if you swallow it | It is harmless, so you can taste it
test: Which action is harmful to another person? | Saying thank you | Sharing your crayons | Helping a friend with maths | *Calling a classmate cruel names
exam: Which word best fills the gap: a poison is ____, so keep it away from children? | harmless | helpful | *harmful | cheerful
